shape theory.algebra.structural-weight : theory.branching, theory.mixing.pythagorean {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 16.17 (Probability from Structural Weight).
// At a branch point with coherent outcomes B_1...B_m:
//   P(B_i) = p_i^2 / sum(p_j^2)
//
// Conservation requires total p^2 to be conserved across
// branch points. Each outcome's share of the conserved quantity
// is p_i^2 / p_total^2. This is the only assignment consistent
// with L^2 conservation.
//
// The Born rule: P proportional to p^2. Structural weight p_i is
// analogous to amplitude; probability goes as the square.
// This is a structural result from conservation geometry, not
// an empirical postulate.
//
// Among structurally equivalent branches, probability is uniform.
// Indeterminacy enters only where structure is exhausted.
//
// Derives from: theory.branching, theory.mixing.pythagorean
  """
}
